---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Terminal from '../../components/Terminal.astro';

const description =
  'Install SSSF 2.0, stamp the hidden project footprint, and start with the plan and implement flows.';
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Quickstart"
  description={description}
  current="/docs/quickstart"
  prev={{ href: '/docs/', label: 'Overview' }}
  next={{ href: '/docs/core-concepts', label: 'Core concepts' }}
>
  <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Why</th><th>Checked by</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="cmd">uv</span> + Python 3.11+</td><td>Install and run the CLI</td><td><span class="cmd">sssf doctor</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="cmd">pi</span></td><td>The coding agent for agent phases</td><td><span class="cmd">sssf doctor</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="cmd">bun</span></td><td>Serve the global visualizer</td><td><span class="cmd">sssf doctor</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="cmd">docker</span></td><td>Sandboxed runs (optional with <code>--no-sandbox</code>)</td><td><span class="cmd">sssf sandbox build</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>1 · Install</h2>
  <pre><code>uv tool install sssf</code></pre>
  <p>One global install serves any number of projects. There is no per-project install step.</p>

  <h2>2 · Initialize a project</h2>
  <pre><code>cd your-repo
sssf init</code></pre>
  <p>
    Initialization stamps the hidden <code class="hl">.adws/</code> footprint and registers
    the project. The tree contains the plan, implement, and deploy chains; roster and provider
    config; the database and runtime artifacts; and prompt, spec, and knowledge-base directories.
    Runtime database/session state is gitignored.
  </p>
  <p>
    On a pre-2.0 project, init backs up the visible <code class="hl">adws/</code> tree to
    <code class="hl">sssf-&lt;timestamp&gt;/</code>, warns that custom chains and config are not
    migrated, and carries forward only the SQLite database. Reapply desired customizations from
    the backup. A flow on an un-upgraded project stops and tells you to run init.
  </p>

  <h2>3 · Capture and plan a ticket</h2>
  <pre><code>sssf ticket new "Explore dark mode"
sssf flow plan</code></pre>
  <p>
    Work always belongs to a ticket. <code class="hl">ticket new</code> captures a title-only
    idea; <code class="hl">flow plan</code> explores, writes the spec, and creates
    <code class="hl">ready-for-agent</code> implementation tickets. To plan a known idea, pass its
    ticket id: <code class="hl">sssf flow plan &lt;ticket-id&gt;</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>4 · Implement and inspect</h2>
  <pre><code>sssf flow implement &lt;ticket-id&gt;
sssf flow implement afk
sssf viz</code></pre>
  <p>
    Implement runs one ready-for-agent ticket through triage, build, and review.
    <code class="hl">afk</code> works the queue one ticket per run. The visualizer provides the
    board, history, and traces. External tracker tickets are pulled and mirrored only when you run
    <code class="hl">sssf ticket sync</code> (or use the board's sync button).
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 26px;">
    <Terminal
      title="sssf 2.0 quickstart"
      lines={[
        { kind: 'prompt', text: '❯ uv tool install sssf' },
        { kind: 'out', text: '✓ installed sssf 2.0.0' },
        { kind: 'prompt', text: '❯ sssf init' },
        { kind: 'out', text: '✓ stamped .adws/ · registered <repo>' },
        { kind: 'prompt', text: '❯ sssf ticket new "Explore dark mode"' },
        { kind: 'out', text: '✓ ticket captured · needs-triage' },
        { kind: 'prompt', text: '❯ sssf flow plan' },
        { kind: 'out', text: '✓ plan landed · implementation tickets ready' },
        { kind: 'prompt', text: '❯ sssf viz' },
        { kind: 'out', text: '→ http://localhost:4600/#/status' },
      ]}
    />
  </div>

  <h2>Sanity check</h2>
  <pre><code>sssf doctor</code></pre>
  <p>Doctor reports the global prerequisites and paths it resolved.</p>
</DocsLayout>
